<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Milan is a major city of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> it served as an imperial residence, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-milan">Edict of Milan</a> of 313 granted toleration to Christians. Carpets from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a>'s workshops are now held in collections in cities including Milan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milan.jpg" alt="Milan" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jiuguang Wang · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Milan_Cathedral_from_Piazza_del_Duomo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
